B.a4J=new A.cy("What is this tool?","This calculator determines if the AW139 bleed valve closing point is within the acceptable NG range for the current temperature, and calculates any adjustment required.",null)
B.a4n=new A.cy("1 \u2014 Enter Temperature","Enter the ambient temperature in \xb0C at the time of the check. Valid range: -50 to 50 \xb0C.\n\nTip: use the mouse scroll wheel on the field to increment/decrement by 1 \xb0C.",null)
B.a4A=new A.cy("2 \u2014 Enter Engine NG","Enter the NG (%) at which the bleed valve closed during the engine run. Valid range: 78.5 to 94.3 %.\n\nTip: scroll wheel changes the value by 0.1 % increments.",null)
B.a4K=new A.cy("3 \u2014 Read the Chart","The chart shows the acceptable range between the red and green curves:\n\u2022 Red curve \u2014 minimum acceptable NG\n\u2022 Green curve \u2014 maximum acceptable NG\n\u2022 Blue vertical line \u2014 current temperature\n\u2022 Blue horizontal line \u2014 current NG reading\n\nTap the chart to open a full-screen zoomable view.",null)
B.a4H=new A.cy("4 \u2014 Read the Result","If the NG is within the band: no adjustment needed.\n\nIf outside:\n\u2022 NG too HIGH (closes too late) \u2192 CCW adjustment\n\u2022 NG too LOW (closes too early) \u2192 CW adjustment\n\n1 flat \u2248 1.3% NG change. Maximum 2 flats per adjustment.",null)
B.a4G=new A.cy("5 \u2014 Share PDF","Once a valid temperature is entered, a share button appears. Tap it to generate and share a PDF report with the chart and adjustment instructions.",null)
B.a4p=new A.cy("Safety","Always refer to up-to-date official AW139 maintenance publications before performing any adjustment. This tool is for reference only.",null)
